  {
    "id": "x402-ext-echo-payment-identifier",
    "intent": "x402-exact",
    "mode": "build-transaction",
    "description": "(a) Client echoes a server-advertised payment-identifier (info.required=true) and populates a fresh client-side id. The outbound v2 PAYMENT-SIGNATURE carries extensions['payment-identifier'].info with required=true preserved and a generated pay_-shaped id matching ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,128}$ (rust PaymentExtensions::echoing + with_payment_identifier_id; coinbase x402 v2 §5.1.2 echo-and-append). The schema field the server published is echoed verbatim. Offer per scheme_exact_svm.md: extra.feePayer is required, decimals come from the mint account (fixture RPC), and the client builds and signs a real transfer.",
    "input": {
      "x402Version": 2,
      "x402Offer": {
        "scheme": "exact",
        "network": "solana:EtWTRABZaYq6iMfeYKouRu166VU2xqa1",
